ddns-clients (0.0.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed settings: interval is now resolve_interval, and refresh_interval
    is now cache_expire, which can also be set per provider. Configs using
    the old names fail to load.
  * New tick setting (default 15 seconds): failed updates are retried at the
    next tick, and the public addresses are looked up at the first tick
    after resolve_interval, whatever the providers' state.
  * The top-level ipv4 and ipv6 settings decide which public addresses are
    looked up; a provider can't enable a family disabled there.
  * A family whose lookup finds nothing keeps its last known addresses, so a
    failed lookup no longer removes its records.
  * max_records keeps the addresses that already have a record first.
  * A provider that rejects the credentials is no longer updated until ddnsd
    is restarted; the others keep running. After server errors or rate
    limiting, No-IP (30 minutes) and Cloudflare (1 to 5 minutes) are given
    time before the next update.
  * Changes of the public addresses are logged, and so is a domain found up
    to date.

 -- XiaoGuang Zeng <xgzeng@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 02:10:59 -0500

ddns-clients (0.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New OpenWrt packages for OpenWrt 25.12 and later.
  * HTTP resolvers: new url setting for both address families, overridden by
    ipv4_url and ipv6_url; each family now connects only over that family. An
    http resolver without any URL is now an error.
  * A domain that doesn't end with its zone gets the zone appended, and an
    empty domain is the zone's root. domain and zone must now be valid DNS
    names.
  * New configuration reference, /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/configuration.md.gz.

 -- XiaoGuang Zeng <xgzeng@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:20:54 -0500

ddns-clients (0.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The config file is now TOML: /etc/ddnsd.toml replaces /etc/ddnsd.yaml.
  * Update any number of providers, as [provider.<name>] tables; a provider
    that rejects its updates is dropped while the others keep running.
  * New settings: replace_only (only re-point existing records) and
    refresh_interval (re-read records hourly, warning about changes made
    elsewhere).
  * New dry-run command, showing what an update would change.
  * No-IP: read the current records from No-IP's nameservers.

 -- XiaoGuang Zeng <xgzeng@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:26:31 -0400

